WEBVTT

00:20.222 --> 00:22.857
<i>("TAKE ME AS I AM" PLAYING)</i>

00:31.199 --> 00:32.433
<i>♪ I've been lookin' too hard ♪</i>

00:32.466 --> 00:33.768
<i>♪ For a home on the top ♪</i>

00:33.801 --> 00:36.271
<i>♪ On the top</i>
<i>of the surface searchin' ♪</i>

00:36.305 --> 00:37.906
<i>♪ Lookin' for something deep ♪</i>

00:37.940 --> 00:39.174
<i>♪ Thought "It's too hard to reach" ♪</i>

00:39.207 --> 00:41.575
<i>♪ Never thought</i>
<i>I was someone deservin' ♪</i>

00:41.609 --> 00:43.178
<i>♪ But it was all in my head ♪</i>

00:43.211 --> 00:46.915
<i>♪ Heavy weight on my chest</i>
<i>only ever left me hurtin' ♪</i>

00:46.949 --> 00:49.952
<i>♪ Now I'm callin' a truce</i>
<i>on the war in my mind ♪</i>

00:49.985 --> 00:52.486
<i>♪ 'Cause I'm finally learnin' I'm not ♪</i>

00:52.520 --> 00:55.057
<i>♪ Rollin' over, under inside out ♪</i>

00:55.090 --> 00:57.858
<i>♪ Turnin' myself</i>
<i>all the way around ♪</i>

00:57.892 --> 01:01.729
<i>♪ What you see</i>
<i>is what you get, so ♪</i>

01:01.762 --> 01:05.599
<i>♪ Baby, you can take me ♪</i>

01:05.633 --> 01:11.605
<i>♪ As I am ♪</i>

01:12.506 --> 01:16.544
<i>♪ Cause' I know I'ma take me ♪</i>

01:16.577 --> 01:22.050
<i>♪ As I am ♪</i>

01:22.084 --> 01:24.920
<i>♪ You can take it or leave it</i>
<i>You can take it or leave it ♪</i>

01:34.229 --> 01:35.529
Wow.

01:44.000 --> 01:48.000
<b>*** Subtitles by dylux ***</b>

01:48.910 --> 01:49.978
Hi, Millie!

01:50.012 --> 01:52.381
Hi, Mrs. Winchester!

01:52.414 --> 01:53.448
So nice to meet you.

01:53.482 --> 01:54.715
Please call me Nina.

01:54.749 --> 01:56.684
I've got some tea for us
and a charcuterie board.

01:56.717 --> 01:58.086
Is it too early
for meat and cheese?

01:58.120 --> 02:01.522
You know, that's what they have
for breakfast in Europe.

02:02.623 --> 02:05.659
MILLIE: Wow, um, you're just,
this is...

02:06.461 --> 02:08.463
I... I...

02:08.497 --> 02:11.832
I'm just going to say, I think
you might be overqualified for this job

02:11.866 --> 02:14.102
with all this experience
and a college degree.

02:14.136 --> 02:15.170
No, I know.

02:15.203 --> 02:18.006
I just realized I really
enjoy being a housemaid.

02:18.040 --> 02:18.907
You do?

02:18.940 --> 02:21.076
For the right families, of course.

02:21.977 --> 02:25.313
Okay. What brought you back
to New York?

02:25.347 --> 02:26.847
I missed it.

02:26.881 --> 02:30.018
Well, I really love New England,
but I miss being in the city.

02:30.052 --> 02:33.721
But you know this is
a live-in position, right?

02:33.754 --> 02:35.656
I mentioned that in the ad,
didn't I?

02:35.689 --> 02:37.292
Oh, yes. Oh, yeah.
No, of course. Yes. Yes.

02:37.325 --> 02:38.759
Oh, God, okay.

02:38.793 --> 02:40.561
- <i>(EXCLAIMS)</i>
- I miss being near the city,

02:40.594 --> 02:42.330
not actually in the city.

02:42.364 --> 02:43.798
It's a little crazy.

02:43.831 --> 02:47.035
Yes, I fully agree with you.

02:47.069 --> 02:50.072
Okay, so the job is
mostly organizing, cleaning,

02:50.105 --> 02:51.772
light cooking, if you're up for that.

02:51.806 --> 02:53.308
Oh, absolutely. I love to cook.

02:53.341 --> 02:54.675
Amazing.

02:54.708 --> 02:56.211
And then you would be
helping me with my daughter.

02:56.244 --> 02:58.579
She's Cecilia, Cece.

02:58.612 --> 03:01.550
She's seven years old
and, well, she's amazing.

03:01.582 --> 03:03.185
Well, I can't wait
to meet her.

03:03.651 --> 03:05.786
Oh. Good. Okay.

03:05.820 --> 03:07.655
Would you like a grand tour

03:07.688 --> 03:09.524
so you can...

03:09.558 --> 03:11.460
see what you're getting yourself into?

03:11.493 --> 03:12.693
Sure.

03:12.726 --> 03:15.397
NINA: And the kitchen.

03:15.430 --> 03:19.534
My husband, Andrew, designed
this entire house soup to nuts.

03:19.568 --> 03:20.701
He's an architect?

03:20.734 --> 03:22.003
No, he's in tech.

03:22.037 --> 03:24.638
But he pays
incredible attention

03:24.672 --> 03:25.974
to every detail.

03:26.007 --> 03:29.511
Now, these steps are, uh,
kind of nuts, I know.

03:29.544 --> 03:32.280
Andrew says I'm totally gonna
kill myself one day on these.

03:32.813 --> 03:34.316
I'm such a klutz.

03:34.349 --> 03:36.817
I should just draw
my chalk outline on the bottom

03:36.851 --> 03:37.953
and get it over with.

03:37.986 --> 03:39.254
So there's another set
of stairs

03:39.287 --> 03:40.322
on the other side of the house

03:40.355 --> 03:42.090
that are less Guggenheim-y.

03:42.124 --> 03:43.391
If you're into that.

03:47.596 --> 03:48.729
Wow.

03:48.762 --> 03:50.764
NINA: It's basically
Andrew's man cave,

03:50.798 --> 03:54.402
but you are welcome to use it
anytime you want, of course.

03:54.436 --> 03:55.669
You'd be part of the family,

03:55.703 --> 03:57.705
which also means
that you would definitely have

03:57.738 --> 03:59.174
to listen to his TED Talk

03:59.207 --> 04:03.378
about how <i>Barry Lyndon</i> is
a misunderstood masterpiece.

04:05.646 --> 04:07.681
This is the upper living room,

04:07.715 --> 04:10.185
which we barely ever use,
to be honest.

04:10.218 --> 04:12.720
You sure you even need a housekeeper?

04:12.753 --> 04:15.524
Well, actually, I'm... expecting.

04:15.557 --> 04:17.592
So I'm not gonna have
quite so much time

04:17.626 --> 04:19.561
to keep everything so perfect.

04:19.594 --> 04:22.330
But don't tell Andrew
because it's very early

04:22.364 --> 04:25.600
and I want to be sure,
you know, before I tell him.

04:25.634 --> 04:27.202
Yeah. Congrats.

04:27.235 --> 04:28.303
Thank you.

04:29.404 --> 04:31.239
This is Cece's room.

04:31.273 --> 04:32.240
Andrew even made a little

04:32.274 --> 04:34.808
miniature version
of our house for her.

04:34.842 --> 04:36.311
- Isn't that sweet?
- Wow.

04:42.584 --> 04:44.718
NINA: So the laundry room is
in the basement,

04:44.752 --> 04:47.489
and that would be
your bathroom

04:47.522 --> 04:49.723
and you would be upstairs.

04:51.226 --> 04:53.295
You're gonna think
it's a little bit small,

04:53.328 --> 04:55.263
but it's got a lot of privacy,

04:55.297 --> 04:57.532
and we figured that that was
the most important thing.

04:57.566 --> 04:59.634
Lots of light, though.

04:59.668 --> 05:00.868
Ta-da!

05:00.902 --> 05:02.770
You can make it your own,
of course.

05:02.803 --> 05:05.173
You can hang posters
and bring in potted plants.

05:05.207 --> 05:07.075
You can blast your music
as loud as you want

05:07.108 --> 05:09.843
because we cannot
hear you downstairs.

05:09.877 --> 05:11.146
What do you think?

05:12.713 --> 05:14.349
- It's perfect.
- Okay, good.

05:15.550 --> 05:16.884
Win!

05:16.918 --> 05:18.520
Well, I'm still interviewing,

05:18.553 --> 05:20.989
but I'm hoping
to make a decision soon.

05:22.057 --> 05:23.458
Here you go.

05:23.491 --> 05:24.526
Oh, no, you don't
have to do that.

05:24.559 --> 05:25.660
Oh, no, I insist.

05:25.694 --> 05:26.827
You spent your energy
and your time

05:26.860 --> 05:28.463
and your gas money
to be here. Please.

05:29.531 --> 05:30.932
I appreciate it.

05:30.966 --> 05:34.369
I have a really good feeling
about this, Millie. I do.

05:34.402 --> 05:35.937
Me too.

05:35.971 --> 05:37.539
Okay. I'll be in touch.

05:37.572 --> 05:38.839
<i>(INAUDIBLE)</i>

05:38.872 --> 05:40.208
MILLIE: <i>She won't be in touch.</i>

05:40.242 --> 05:43.411
<i>That's the last time I'll ever</i>
<i>set foot in that house.</i>

05:43.445 --> 05:44.878
<i>One background check,</i>

05:44.913 --> 05:47.983
<i>and she'll see that everything</i>
<i>on that resume is a total lie.</i>

05:48.016 --> 05:49.817
<i>I don't even wear glasses.</i>

05:49.850 --> 05:51.785
<i>I'm just...</i>
<i>I'm trying to look legit.</i>

05:51.819 --> 05:53.088
<i>So stupid.</i>

05:59.827 --> 06:01.396
<i>(HAND DRYER BLOWING)</i>

06:07.636 --> 06:09.337
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

06:12.040 --> 06:13.642
Um, can I get a job application?

06:13.675 --> 06:15.343
Yeah, sure.

06:15.377 --> 06:17.078
- There you go.
- Thanks.

06:25.687 --> 06:26.921
<i>(HAND DRYER BLOWING)</i>

06:27.756 --> 06:29.391
MILLIE: <i>I knew she wouldn't call.</i>

06:29.424 --> 06:31.326
<i>Why did I even think I had</i>
<i>a shot at that job?</i>

06:31.359 --> 06:34.362
<i>Oh, well, at least I got</i>
<i>$20 out of it.</i>

06:35.964 --> 06:38.133
<i>(SIGHS) I don't know</i>
<i>what I'm gonna do.</i>

06:48.310 --> 06:49.344
Roll it down.

06:51.780 --> 06:53.281
Can't sleep here.

06:53.315 --> 06:55.016
I'm so sorry. I...

06:55.050 --> 06:56.618
I was driving from my mom's house

06:56.651 --> 06:57.986
and I got really sleepy,

06:58.019 --> 06:59.721
and I just I pulled over
to take a nap. I'm sorry.

06:59.754 --> 07:02.190
<i>(PHONE VIBRATING)</i>

07:02.223 --> 07:03.925
This is her actually.
Do you mind if I take it?

07:03.958 --> 07:05.293
She's probably freaking out.

07:05.327 --> 07:06.795
Don't text and drive.

07:06.827 --> 07:08.263
I won't. I promise.

07:11.433 --> 07:13.935
- Hello?
- <i>Hi, may I speak to Millie?</i>

07:13.968 --> 07:16.604
Uh, this is her. She.

07:16.638 --> 07:18.373
<i>This is Nina Winchester.</i>

07:18.406 --> 07:20.375
<i>I'm calling to offer you the job.</i>

07:20.408 --> 07:23.011
<i>I mean, if you're</i>
<i>still available.</i>

07:23.044 --> 07:24.979
<i>Uh, you've probably got</i>
<i>a million job offers.</i>

07:25.013 --> 07:27.048
No. I mean, yes, yes.
I would love to.

07:27.082 --> 07:29.250
Uh, when would
you like me to start?

07:29.284 --> 07:32.987
<i>Oh, my goodness. (SIGHS)</i>
<i>As soon as possible?</i>

07:33.021 --> 07:34.456
Well, what about this afternoon?

07:34.489 --> 07:35.690
<i>You know what?</i>

07:35.724 --> 07:37.292
- <i>That would be great.</i>
- Great.

07:37.325 --> 07:39.127
<i>Anyway, gotta run.</i>
<i>Bye, Millie.</i>

07:39.661 --> 07:41.029
MILLIE: <i>(SOFTLY)</i> Yes!

07:49.904 --> 07:52.507
- <i>(CLICK)</i>
- <i>(LINE RINGING)</i>

07:55.076 --> 07:56.144
Hey!

07:57.645 --> 07:58.747
- Hey, I'm Millie.
- <i>(LINE RINGING)</i>

07:58.780 --> 08:01.282
Do you work for the Winchesters?

08:01.316 --> 08:03.818
I'm trying to get in,
but I don't know the code.

08:03.852 --> 08:04.885
<i>(LINE BEEPS)</i>

08:04.919 --> 08:06.154
<i>(GATES CLANK)</i>

08:30.145 --> 08:31.179
Nina?

08:33.047 --> 08:34.482
Nina, it's Millie.

08:40.422 --> 08:41.456
Nina?

08:50.498 --> 08:52.600
NINA: Millie? Millie, Millie, Millie!

08:53.435 --> 08:54.803
<i>(EXCLAIMS)</i> Welcome. Hi.

08:54.836 --> 08:56.738
Sorry. I, um, meant
to leave the gate open.

08:56.771 --> 08:59.674
Do you need me to help you bring
in your stuff from your car?

08:59.707 --> 09:01.009
Oh, no, this is it.

09:01.042 --> 09:03.178
- Great. Wow.
- Yeah.

09:03.211 --> 09:04.846
Yeah, no, I put the rest of it
in a storage unit.

09:04.879 --> 09:07.282
Okay, well, that's great.
I'm gonna put these up in your room.

09:07.315 --> 09:10.185
Listen, I need to write a PTA speech

09:10.218 --> 09:12.287
that has to be a barn burner,

09:12.320 --> 09:13.755
so I'm gonna be stuck in my office.

09:13.788 --> 09:15.990
But the cleaning supplies are
in this closet over there,

09:16.424 --> 09:18.660
and... um, oh.

09:18.693 --> 09:20.662
You're not wearing
your glasses.

09:20.695 --> 09:23.731
Oh, I don't... I don't wear 'em
all the time. Contacts.

09:25.400 --> 09:26.501
Oh.

09:26.534 --> 09:28.369
Yeah, you look better without them.

09:29.304 --> 09:30.472
Yeah. Okay.

09:30.972 --> 09:33.074
I'll be upstairs.

09:33.107 --> 09:34.576
This is gonna be fun, Millie!

09:34.609 --> 09:36.611
<i>("TUMBLING DICE"
BY LINDA RONSTADT PLAYING)</i>

09:40.648 --> 09:45.019
<i>♪ People try to rape me</i>
<i>Always think I'm crazy ♪</i>

09:45.053 --> 09:48.690
<i>♪ Make me burn</i>
<i>the candle right down ♪</i>

09:49.925 --> 09:51.826
<i>♪ Baby ♪</i>

09:51.860 --> 09:53.929
<i>(SONG CONTINUES PLAYING
ON HEADPHONES)</i>

09:53.963 --> 09:55.697
No shoes on the furniture.

09:59.400 --> 10:02.003
Um, hey. Hi.

10:02.036 --> 10:04.772
You must be... Cece.

10:05.440 --> 10:06.674
I'm Millie.

10:07.475 --> 10:08.510
Hello.

10:09.244 --> 10:11.579
Oh, hey. Hi! You met Millie.

10:11.613 --> 10:12.447
Hi, baby.

10:12.480 --> 10:14.549
Millie's gonna be living with us,

10:14.582 --> 10:15.416
and she's gonna be helping

10:15.450 --> 10:16.751
with the cooking and the cleaning.

10:16.784 --> 10:17.987
And you know what?

10:18.052 --> 10:19.521
She might even play
<i>Candy Land</i> with you

10:19.554 --> 10:21.789
if you ask her
with a pretty please.

10:21.823 --> 10:23.291
She's gonna live with us?

10:23.324 --> 10:25.727
<i>(LAUGHING)</i> Yes.
Andrew, I told you that.

10:25.760 --> 10:29.932
I said she was gonna be living
in the guest room in the attic.

10:29.965 --> 10:32.433
Doesn't this place look
incredible. Look at it.

10:35.069 --> 10:37.672
- Thank you.
- Well, Millie, welcome.

10:37.705 --> 10:39.073
Uh, thank you.

10:39.107 --> 10:40.408
Are you hungry?
I'm sure we can

10:40.441 --> 10:42.011
turn this dinner for three
into a dinner for four.

10:42.043 --> 10:44.112
No, I'm probably
just gonna go upstairs

10:44.145 --> 10:46.447
and, uh, get all settled in.

10:46.481 --> 10:47.682
- You sure?
- If you don't mind,

10:47.715 --> 10:50.251
I'll just come down afterwards
and tidy up.

10:50.285 --> 10:52.420
Yeah, get settled.
Yeah, take your time.

10:52.453 --> 10:53.923
We're so happy that you're here.

10:53.956 --> 10:55.557
You just let us know
if you change your mind.

10:56.491 --> 10:57.559
Thanks.

11:02.764 --> 11:04.832
You ordered from the wrong
Italian place again.

11:41.036 --> 11:42.270
NINA: Knock, knock.

11:43.638 --> 11:44.472
Hi.

11:44.505 --> 11:46.674
That window doesn't open, sadly.

11:46.708 --> 11:48.576
But there's a lot
of ventilation in this room,

11:48.610 --> 11:50.612
so you should never
get stuffy in here.

11:50.645 --> 11:51.981
I got you some dinner.

11:52.014 --> 11:54.682
Andrew always over-orders.

11:54.716 --> 11:55.650
I put some water

11:55.683 --> 11:57.019
in the mini fridge,
did you see that?

11:57.052 --> 11:58.686
Yeah, I really don't
want to be a pain,

11:58.720 --> 12:01.422
but if it is possible to try
and get the window open,

12:01.456 --> 12:03.591
it'd be nice to get
some fresh air in here.

12:03.625 --> 12:06.127
Yeah, I agree.
That's a great idea.

12:06.160 --> 12:07.895
I will talk to the handyman
about that.

12:07.930 --> 12:10.598
Okay, cool. Is that the guy
that's down in the yard?

12:10.632 --> 12:12.800
No, that's Enzo.
He's the groundskeeper.

12:12.834 --> 12:14.168
Never mind him.

12:14.202 --> 12:16.204
And then if I could just
get a key for the deadbolt.

12:16.237 --> 12:19.173
Oh, my God, yes. The deadbolt.

12:19.207 --> 12:22.011
<i>(CHUCKLES)</i> That's so creepy.

12:22.044 --> 12:25.847
This used to be Andrew's storage
closet for his files. Okay?

12:25.880 --> 12:27.315
But, oh, my God,

12:27.815 --> 12:29.717
closed window, deadbolt.

12:31.386 --> 12:33.022
What kind of monsters are we?

12:33.055 --> 12:34.889
- Uh...
- I will sort that out.

12:34.923 --> 12:36.591
Oh, before I forget. Um...

12:38.192 --> 12:39.827
This is for you. A present.

12:39.861 --> 12:42.931
Also, just, I saw that your
phone was just really ancient,

12:42.965 --> 12:45.199
and I wanted you to have that

12:45.233 --> 12:48.070
because I uploaded
the credit card onto it

12:48.103 --> 12:49.138
so you can use it
at the grocery store

12:49.170 --> 12:50.438
and for gas.

12:50.471 --> 12:52.874
Oh, um, I'll take good care
of it. Thank you.

12:52.908 --> 12:58.279
Honestly, I'm like, so happy that...
you're here with us.

12:58.947 --> 13:00.314
Thanks.

13:00.348 --> 13:01.883
Can I give you a hug?

13:03.851 --> 13:05.720
<i>(SIGHS)</i> Thank you, Millie.

13:05.753 --> 13:07.722
Thank you. Okay.

13:07.755 --> 13:09.590
Let me know if you need anything else.

13:27.208 --> 13:28.609
<i>(YAWNS)</i>

13:34.917 --> 13:35.951
Shit.

13:44.193 --> 13:45.426
<i>(CLICKS)</i>

13:45.928 --> 13:48.629
<i>(LOCK RATTLES)</i>

13:48.663 --> 13:49.497
No, no, no.

13:49.530 --> 13:51.934
- <i>(STRAINING)</i>
- <i>(DOORKNOB RATTLING)</i>

13:51.967 --> 13:53.334
No, no, no.

13:53.835 --> 13:55.336
<i>(DOOR CREAKS)</i>

13:58.239 --> 13:59.474
<i>(SHRIEKING)</i>

14:06.949 --> 14:08.449
Nina?

14:08.483 --> 14:10.418
- <i>(SHOUTING)</i> Where are they?
- Where are what?

14:10.451 --> 14:12.620
My PTA notes
for the meeting tonight!

14:12.653 --> 14:14.089
They were right here
on the counter,

14:14.123 --> 14:15.224
and now they're not here.

14:15.256 --> 14:16.657
- Where are they?
- I didn't see any notes.

14:16.691 --> 14:17.926
Bullshit!

14:17.960 --> 14:18.994
Where are they?

14:20.229 --> 14:21.997
- Nina, no, no.
- ANDREW: Hey.

14:22.030 --> 14:23.331
Hey! What's going on?

14:23.364 --> 14:27.035
Millie threw away my notes
for the meeting tonight.

14:28.569 --> 14:30.471
<i>(SHOUTING)</i> Where are they?

14:32.273 --> 14:34.209
Nina, why don't we go
check your office?

14:34.243 --> 14:36.111
I have to get up and do a speech

14:36.145 --> 14:37.345
in front of everybody

14:37.378 --> 14:38.679
and now I have nothing!

14:38.713 --> 14:41.150
- <i>(OBJECTS CLATTERING)</i>
- <i>(SHRIEKING)</i>

14:41.183 --> 14:42.951
- ANDREW: Nina!
- <i>(YELLING)</i> What?

14:42.985 --> 14:45.220
- <i>(DRAWER SLIDING SHUT)</i>
- <i>(THUDS)</i>

14:45.254 --> 14:47.455
- Do you have a copy...
- <i>(VESSELS CLINKING)</i>

14:48.023 --> 14:49.258
on your computer?

14:49.290 --> 14:51.392
I wrote them by hand!

14:51.927 --> 14:53.561
Oh, fuck!

14:53.594 --> 14:55.897
I always think better
when I write by hand.

14:55.931 --> 14:57.465
Where's my nail at?

14:58.066 --> 14:59.634
<i>(SHRIEKS AND WHIMPERS)</i>

15:00.202 --> 15:04.539
<i>(CRYING)</i>

15:04.572 --> 15:06.175
ANDREW: All right.
Come here, come here.

15:06.208 --> 15:08.342
- <i>(CRYING)</i>
- It's okay.

15:09.811 --> 15:13.182
<i>(CRYING)</i>

15:13.215 --> 15:15.449
ANDREW: Let's take
a deep breath, okay?

15:15.483 --> 15:17.718
- <i>(NINA CONTINUES CRYING)</i>
- Breathe, breathe, breathe.

15:17.752 --> 15:20.189
- Breathe, breathe, breathe.
- <i>(SNIFFLES)</i>

15:20.222 --> 15:22.423
<i>(EXHALES AND SNIFFLES)</i>

15:23.025 --> 15:24.325
I'm gonna pick you up.

15:27.395 --> 15:28.696
- <i>(NINA CRIES)</i>
- <i>(ANDREW GRUNTS SOFTLY)</i>

15:28.729 --> 15:30.966
<i>(NINA SOBBING)</i>

15:35.037 --> 15:38.040
Here's the plan. I am going
to take Cece to school,

15:38.073 --> 15:39.774
and you...

15:39.807 --> 15:42.211
you are going to take
a hot shower.

15:42.244 --> 15:43.744
You're gonna have
a nice long breakfast,

15:43.778 --> 15:45.680
and then you have all day
to work on your speech,

15:45.713 --> 15:48.984
and you can still make it
to the salon for a touch up.

15:49.017 --> 15:50.953
You'll have just enough time
to get your roots done.

15:50.986 --> 15:52.187
I love you so much.

15:52.221 --> 15:53.588
- I love you.
- I love you.

15:56.657 --> 15:58.927
You need to be
more careful next time.

16:01.029 --> 16:02.697
You've ruined my entire day.

16:04.365 --> 16:05.600
I'm sorry.

16:10.805 --> 16:12.040
<i>(ANDREW SIGHS)</i>

16:14.442 --> 16:15.676
I am so sorry.

16:16.979 --> 16:18.080
Don-- Don't worry about it.

16:18.113 --> 16:19.814
I don't know what's been
going on with her lately.

16:19.847 --> 16:21.449
She's...

16:21.482 --> 16:24.119
she's been on a real
emotional roller coaster.

16:24.152 --> 16:25.887
Oh, it's probably the hor--

16:27.289 --> 16:29.490
um, Mercury in retrograde.

16:29.523 --> 16:31.360
Didn't peg you
for the star-chart type.

16:31.392 --> 16:32.793
Guilty.

16:36.031 --> 16:37.598
Let me help you clean up.

16:37.632 --> 16:39.167
- It's a fuckin' mess in here.
- No, no, no. I got it.

16:39.201 --> 16:41.303
I got it. You go get ready.

16:41.336 --> 16:42.837
I don't want you
to be late for Cece.

16:43.939 --> 16:45.040
Thank you.

16:47.976 --> 16:50.611
- <i>(TAPS COUNTERTOP)</i>
- Tomorrow will be better.

16:52.613 --> 16:54.582
It'll be better, I promise.

16:55.150 --> 16:56.184
Okay.

17:01.689 --> 17:03.258
- Yeah.
- <i>(TAPS COUNTERTOP)</i>

17:03.292 --> 17:05.660
Cece! Let's hit the road!

17:25.914 --> 17:27.515
<i>(IN NON-NATIVE ACCENT)</i>
What are you doing here?

17:28.116 --> 17:29.483
I work here.

17:30.419 --> 17:32.087
What are you doing here?

17:32.988 --> 17:34.522
You...

17:42.530 --> 17:46.500
<i>(MUTTERS IN ITALIAN)</i>

18:02.650 --> 18:04.119
- <i>(YAWNS)</i>
- <i>(BUCKET THUDS)</i>

18:24.739 --> 18:26.475
I don't really fit in very well

18:26.507 --> 18:28.542
with those other PTA moms.

18:29.777 --> 18:32.447
I guess I didn't realize
how stressed I've been.

18:32.481 --> 18:36.084
It's probably just all the new
hormones making you go crazy.

18:38.753 --> 18:40.422
I wouldn't say anything to Andrew.

18:40.455 --> 18:41.789
Get out.

18:42.324 --> 18:43.458
I have to shower.

18:43.492 --> 18:45.327
And you're gonna handle dinner later.

18:45.360 --> 18:46.594
MILLIE: Yeah.

18:47.362 --> 18:48.497
ANDREW: It smells amazing.

18:48.529 --> 18:50.332
MILLIE: It's chicken piccata.

18:50.365 --> 18:51.599
ANDREW: Mmm.

18:51.632 --> 18:53.834
Oh, I picked this up for Cece.

18:53.868 --> 18:56.804
Oh, these are fantastic.
She's gonna love these.

18:56.837 --> 18:58.040
Someone did not
get her snack today,

18:58.073 --> 19:00.442
and she's a very hungry
little ballerina.

19:00.475 --> 19:01.943
<i>(MILLIE CHUCKLES SOFTLY)</i>

19:01.977 --> 19:04.413
Why don't you get her started,
and I'll be right back down?

19:04.446 --> 19:05.846
Okay.

19:08.350 --> 19:09.650
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

19:11.585 --> 19:13.021
Hey, Cece,

19:13.388 --> 19:14.722
how was class?

19:16.258 --> 19:17.426
<i>(BREATHES DEEPLY)</i>

19:17.459 --> 19:20.861
Would you, uh, like juice
or... or water?

19:20.895 --> 19:23.631
Juice.
But this glass is dirty.

19:24.565 --> 19:26.334
Really? I just took it out
of the dishwasher.

19:26.368 --> 19:27.635
Juice is a privilege.

19:27.668 --> 19:30.105
Not something you drink
out of a dirty glass.

19:31.540 --> 19:32.807
Of course not.

19:34.109 --> 19:35.143
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

19:46.254 --> 19:47.989
This looks amazing.

19:48.023 --> 19:50.926
Doesn't it, Cece? Way better
than dinosaur nuggets.

19:52.626 --> 19:54.162
Hey, Millie,

19:54.196 --> 19:57.065
why don't you grab
a place setting and join us?

19:58.066 --> 19:59.101
Uh...

19:59.134 --> 20:00.569
No, I... I already ate.

20:00.601 --> 20:01.869
Oh, we insist.

20:02.703 --> 20:04.172
Don't we, Cece?

20:06.441 --> 20:07.675
Um...

20:08.709 --> 20:10.345
I hope you guys like it.

20:30.332 --> 20:31.933
<i>(KNOCKING AT DOOR)</i>

20:33.101 --> 20:34.236
Come in.

20:36.605 --> 20:38.607
Hey.

20:38.639 --> 20:40.808
- Hey.
- Sorry to bother you.

20:42.310 --> 20:43.644
Got something for you.

20:43.677 --> 20:45.046
Cece insisted.

20:45.914 --> 20:47.949
- She's so sweet.
- Yeah.

20:50.152 --> 20:53.088
<i>("WHY IS SHE STILL HERE?"
BY RENEE RAPP PLAYING)</i>

20:56.992 --> 20:59.361
<i>♪ You can tell me ♪</i>

20:59.394 --> 21:01.196
<i>♪ You don't love her ♪</i>

21:01.229 --> 21:04.499
<i>♪ But you should</i>
<i>probably tell her too ♪</i>

21:04.533 --> 21:05.634
<i>♪ 'Cause I can't keep... ♪</i>

21:05.666 --> 21:06.935
<i>(GASPS)</i>

21:07.435 --> 21:08.669
No, no, no.

21:08.702 --> 21:11.039
Absolutely fucking not!

21:12.073 --> 21:13.108
Oh, my God.

21:21.815 --> 21:24.019
I want you to feel safe here.

21:26.087 --> 21:27.122
I do.

21:29.890 --> 21:31.792
For your door, as requested.

21:32.327 --> 21:33.861
Thanks.

21:37.465 --> 21:39.800
So how was last night?
With Andrew?

21:41.236 --> 21:42.703
Good.

21:42.736 --> 21:44.372
I made chicken piccata.

21:45.574 --> 21:47.375
He's a dream, isn't he?

21:48.876 --> 21:50.679
He pretends to like everything
I make him,

21:50.711 --> 21:51.947
even if he hates it.

21:57.485 --> 21:58.752
Mmm.

22:01.456 --> 22:03.425
That's a lot of bacon, Millie.

22:03.458 --> 22:05.160
Are you trying to kill us?

22:10.764 --> 22:12.133
Where are you going?

22:14.402 --> 22:15.604
I have...

22:15.637 --> 22:16.938
Saturday off.

22:16.972 --> 22:18.073
Isn't that
what we talked about?

22:18.106 --> 22:21.109
No, I...
I can't spare you today.

22:21.977 --> 22:24.012
I missed my hair salon appointment

22:24.045 --> 22:27.482
because you threw away
my notes. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

22:27.515 --> 22:29.117
Remember?

22:29.150 --> 22:32.220
I have a meeting that I can't miss.

22:32.254 --> 22:33.521
<i>(SCOFFS)</i>

22:33.555 --> 22:34.923
You have a meeting?

22:35.490 --> 22:36.925
What's the meeting for?

22:39.760 --> 22:41.396
If I could just have
a couple hours off,

22:41.429 --> 22:42.464
and then I'll come back.

22:42.497 --> 22:44.798
Millie, absolutely not.

22:44.832 --> 22:46.635
- ANDREW: Baby?
- I can't have you... What?

22:46.668 --> 22:48.903
Sweetheart, it's okay.
She can go.

22:50.405 --> 22:52.507
- But, Andy, it's your day off.
- I know, exactly.

22:52.540 --> 22:55.977
And that's why we're gonna go
to the park... fly this kite.

22:56.011 --> 22:57.145
And we've been waiting
all week to fly, right?

22:57.178 --> 22:58.113
We're doing donuts,
we're doing kites,

22:58.146 --> 22:59.847
and then we're doing ballet.

23:01.416 --> 23:02.450
Go. Take your time.

23:06.421 --> 23:08.556
- Bye, Mama.
- Bye, baby.

23:10.791 --> 23:14.062
<i>(BREATHES DEEPLY)</i>

23:14.095 --> 23:15.230
Have fun.

23:19.734 --> 23:21.002
Thanks.

23:23.338 --> 23:24.439
<i>(DOOR OPENS)</i>

23:26.408 --> 23:27.841
PAM: Hey, how are you doin'?

23:27.875 --> 23:29.611
MILLIE: I'm good.

23:29.644 --> 23:31.046
Still writing in your journal?

23:31.079 --> 23:34.015
Uh, yeah. Do you wanna read it?

23:34.049 --> 23:34.949
God, no.

23:34.983 --> 23:37.719
I have enough shit
to read as it is.

23:37.752 --> 23:40.055
So you left the job at Charlie's?

23:40.088 --> 23:43.857
Well, this housekeeping job
just sort of fell into my lap.

23:43.891 --> 23:46.428
And it's live-in,
so I'm saving a fortune on rent.

23:46.461 --> 23:48.496
Okay, that's good.

23:48.530 --> 23:51.399
I have my new address here,

23:51.433 --> 23:52.967
and phone number.

23:53.001 --> 23:55.437
The family is really amazing.

23:55.470 --> 23:56.938
I feel... I feel lucky.

23:56.971 --> 23:59.174
Must make meeting new people
a little tough, though,

23:59.207 --> 24:00.775
having to live with a family.

24:00.809 --> 24:02.177
I mean, you would
think that, right?

24:02.210 --> 24:06.181
But I have already met
a ton of really cool nannies.

24:06.214 --> 24:08.016
Any mannies in there? <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

24:08.917 --> 24:11.786
Are you asking me
about my love life, Pam?

24:11.820 --> 24:13.188
If I know how Tinder works,

24:13.221 --> 24:16.024
or if I'm horn dogging
all over Great Neck

24:16.057 --> 24:17.392
because I haven't gotten laid
in ten years?

24:17.425 --> 24:20.295
No. I'm just saying
human connections are important.

24:21.663 --> 24:22.931
Definitely.

24:22.964 --> 24:25.066
But hold onto this job, Millie.

24:25.767 --> 24:27.168
And the living situation.

24:29.104 --> 24:31.306
You'll need both,
or you'll be back at Bedford

24:31.339 --> 24:34.743
serving the five years
left on your sentence.

24:34.776 --> 24:36.978
And I don't like that for you.

24:37.011 --> 24:39.180
I don't like that for me, either.

24:42.016 --> 24:44.619
<i>(PHONE VIBRATING)</i>

24:48.022 --> 24:49.824
- Hi, Nina, I'm just--
- <i>I need you to pick up Cece</i>

24:49.858 --> 24:52.761
<i>from ballet class, 1:45,</i>
<i>and don't be late.</i>

24:52.794 --> 24:53.995
<i>(LINE DISCONNECTS)</i>

24:54.028 --> 24:57.031
Um, okay, where is it? Nina?

24:58.666 --> 25:00.001
What?

25:01.369 --> 25:02.604
Ballet school?

25:03.037 --> 25:04.272
Ballet class.

25:06.274 --> 25:07.709
Little kids.

25:07.742 --> 25:09.477
Fuck.

25:09.511 --> 25:10.879
INSTRUCTOR: Tendu right.

25:10.912 --> 25:14.382
And curtsy
and open to the left.

25:14.416 --> 25:15.717
Foot behind you.

25:15.750 --> 25:18.253
Excellent, and close to first.

25:18.286 --> 25:20.188
Fabulous class today.
Thank you.

25:20.221 --> 25:22.323
Let's go get
our bags and shoes.

25:22.357 --> 25:24.993
- Great job.
- <i>(DOORBELL CHIMING)</i>

25:26.060 --> 25:29.063
- Hi. Who are you looking for?
- Uh, Cece.

25:29.097 --> 25:30.932
Cecilia Winchester.

25:30.965 --> 25:32.333
Are you Nina's new girl?

25:33.101 --> 25:35.670
- Yes. Hi, I'm Millie.
- Hi.

25:37.005 --> 25:38.273
MILLIE: Hi!

25:38.306 --> 25:41.042
Cece! Hey,
I'm here to pick you up.

25:41.075 --> 25:43.178
I'm spending the night
at Emma's.

25:43.211 --> 25:45.947
We arranged it weeks ago.
She has all her things.

25:45.980 --> 25:47.282
Oh, no, no, no.

25:47.315 --> 25:48.918
Nina just called me
and asked me to pick her up,

25:48.950 --> 25:50.351
so she probably
changed her mind.

25:50.385 --> 25:51.953
PATRICE: Oh.

25:51.986 --> 25:53.655
<i>(EXHALES)</i> Okay, let me check.

25:57.959 --> 25:59.227
Nina!

25:59.694 --> 26:01.931
Hi, it's Patrice.

26:01.963 --> 26:03.832
Your girl is here. She's insisting

26:03.865 --> 26:06.367
she needs to pick up Cece.

26:08.636 --> 26:10.238
<i>(PATRICE CHUCKLES)</i>

26:11.573 --> 26:12.674
I know.

26:13.341 --> 26:14.309
I know.

26:14.342 --> 26:16.311
No, it's no problem at all.

26:16.344 --> 26:18.980
It's impossible to find
reliable help.

26:19.681 --> 26:21.816
Oh, would you like to confirm?

26:21.850 --> 26:23.318
<i>(MILLIE INHALES)</i>

26:24.285 --> 26:25.420
Have fun.

26:27.589 --> 26:28.924
We figured it out.

26:28.958 --> 26:31.559
Okay, take care. Bye.

26:32.327 --> 26:34.295
Wow,
they really are beautiful.

26:34.329 --> 26:36.464
NINA: So happy we'll be able
to use them,

26:36.498 --> 26:37.565
Mother Winchester.

26:37.599 --> 26:40.401
Well, the pattern is vintage,
of course.

26:41.035 --> 26:42.303
NINA: Millie.

26:44.539 --> 26:47.008
I told you Cece was having
a sleepover tonight.

26:47.041 --> 26:49.277
There was no need to make a scene.

26:49.310 --> 26:50.812
- <i>(MILLIE INHALES)</i>
- <i>(MOTHER SIGHS)</i>

26:50.845 --> 26:54.950
This is how you allow the help
to dress in your home?

26:54.984 --> 26:56.986
Uh, this is Andrew's mother,
Mrs. Winchester.

26:57.018 --> 26:58.219
She's downsizing,

26:58.253 --> 27:00.421
so she has brought us
her mother's china.

27:00.455 --> 27:02.156
- Yes.
- NINA: Isn't it lovely?

27:03.491 --> 27:05.059
Isn't it?

27:05.793 --> 27:07.762
- Yes.
- I know.

27:07.795 --> 27:10.398
Andrew loves these dishes.

27:10.966 --> 27:13.034
I want you...

27:13.067 --> 27:14.569
to put them somewhere safe

27:14.602 --> 27:17.305
'cause Nina's likely
to trip over herself

27:17.338 --> 27:19.073
and smash them all to pieces.

27:19.107 --> 27:20.275
- <i>(MOTHER CHUCKLES)</i>
- <i>(DOOR OPENS)</i>

27:20.308 --> 27:22.243
- Guilty as charged.
- <i>(DOOR CLOSES)</i>

27:22.277 --> 27:23.946
- MOTHER: Andrew!
- ANDREW: Oh.

27:23.979 --> 27:26.514
- Mother.
- Oh, Andrew, where's your tie?

27:26.548 --> 27:29.284
ANDREW: I know,
I'm too casual. I'm sorry.

27:29.317 --> 27:31.219
- Your hair is fabulous.
- Thank you, darling.

27:31.252 --> 27:33.421
Not a root in sight. Is...

27:33.454 --> 27:35.089
- Is that what I think it is?
- Yes, it is.

27:35.123 --> 27:37.091
Can't wait to eat off
of those plates.

27:37.125 --> 27:38.793
MOTHER: Family heirlooms.

27:38.826 --> 27:40.762
- So happy it's back.
- Me too.

27:44.566 --> 27:45.833
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

27:47.235 --> 27:49.470
This fucking window.
<i>(GROANS SOFTLY)</i>

27:54.108 --> 27:56.045
<i>(GROANS SOFTLY)</i>

27:56.077 --> 27:57.612
<i>(WOOD SQUEAKING SOFTLY)</i>

28:18.968 --> 28:20.501
<i>(WOMAN SPEAKING ON TV)</i>
<i>Dishes are still in the sink.</i>

28:20.535 --> 28:22.537
MAN 1: <i>Yeah, I know.</i>
<i>I'm kinda lettin' em soak.</i>

28:22.570 --> 28:23.973
WOMAN: <i>Uh,</i>
<i>they've been soaking</i>

28:24.006 --> 28:25.673
- <i>for three days.</i>
- <i>(LAUGH TRACK)</i>

28:25.707 --> 28:27.108
MAN: <i>Well, now,</i>
<i>you know, it's kinda...</i>

28:27.141 --> 28:29.143
<i>Glug, glug, glug,</i>
<i>glug, glug. Ding.</i>

28:29.177 --> 28:30.878
<i>Glug, glug, glug.</i>

28:30.913 --> 28:32.413
<i>...home with everybody going out.</i>

28:33.247 --> 28:34.315
<i>I'm going to ask you one...</i>

28:34.349 --> 28:36.150
<i>(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)</i>

28:37.619 --> 28:39.387
MAN: <i>I'm not gonna ask you</i>
<i>what you sell.</i>

28:39.420 --> 28:41.623
<i>I'm gonna go on here</i>
<i>to Patsy, all right?</i>

28:41.656 --> 28:43.157
ANDREW: Ah, <i>Family Feud.</i>

28:43.591 --> 28:45.259
I'm so sorry.

28:45.293 --> 28:47.062
Um... I...
I couldn't get some...

28:47.096 --> 28:48.329
- I'll leave you alone.
- No, no. Please.

28:48.363 --> 28:49.530
- Get out of your way.
- Sit, please. No, sit.

28:49.564 --> 28:50.832
Come on.

28:52.233 --> 28:53.901
Please stay.

28:53.936 --> 28:56.170
Oh, I love this show.

28:56.638 --> 28:58.339
Me too.

28:58.373 --> 29:00.976
I've only ever seen
the Steve Harvey one.

29:01.010 --> 29:03.078
- Really? Oh, this is classic.
- Yeah.

29:03.112 --> 29:04.579
This is Richard Dawson.

29:04.612 --> 29:06.147
Fashion icon.

29:06.714 --> 29:09.051
- He's an OG.
- Yeah?

29:09.084 --> 29:11.152
He has
some spectacular sideburns.

29:11.185 --> 29:12.854
He sure does.

29:12.887 --> 29:16.025
Man, my family would have
killed on this show.

29:16.058 --> 29:17.825
They are absolute vultures.

29:17.859 --> 29:18.893
Especially my mother.

29:18.927 --> 29:21.229
What about you?
You... your, um...

29:21.262 --> 29:22.730
parents, are they game people?

29:24.133 --> 29:26.734
Oh, we don't really
keep in touch anymore.

29:26.768 --> 29:27.802
Oh.

29:27.835 --> 29:28.870
I'm sorry.

29:29.804 --> 29:31.372
That's gotta be hard.

29:31.406 --> 29:33.775
Uh, not really, no.

29:33.808 --> 29:35.944
I mean, even if we were,
they probably wouldn't...

29:36.644 --> 29:38.246
be into this.

29:38.279 --> 29:40.715
They're kinda like
the opposite of fun.

29:40.748 --> 29:41.849
Well, I'll tell you what.

29:43.152 --> 29:44.619
You can be on our team.

29:45.988 --> 29:47.355
It'd be me and you...

29:48.389 --> 29:50.092
and Nina and my mom.

29:50.125 --> 29:51.927
Nina's parents don't
make the cut?

29:52.593 --> 29:54.495
They died when she was a kid.

29:55.263 --> 29:57.265
- That's awful.
- Yeah.

29:58.133 --> 29:59.734
It's a crazy story, actually.

29:59.767 --> 30:01.302
They died in a house fire.

30:02.236 --> 30:05.140
No one knows how it was started.

30:05.174 --> 30:06.808
Nina made it out,
her parents didn't.

30:06.841 --> 30:09.544
For a long time, the police
actually thought that she...

30:14.083 --> 30:16.018
Can you imagine...

30:16.051 --> 30:18.419
living with that your entire life?

30:18.453 --> 30:20.788
- That'd be terrible.
- What would be terrible?

30:22.323 --> 30:23.558
ANDREW: There she is.

30:23.992 --> 30:25.127
Hey.

30:25.160 --> 30:27.328
RICHARD: <i>Name a cartoon bird.</i>

30:27.930 --> 30:29.131
<i>(BUZZER BEEPING)</i>

30:29.164 --> 30:30.465
What are you doing up?

30:30.498 --> 30:32.433
What do you mean?
I can say the same about you.

30:32.467 --> 30:34.268
I'm watching <i>Family Feud.</i>

30:34.302 --> 30:35.470
NINA: Mmm.

30:35.503 --> 30:37.271
- At 2:00 a.m.?
- You wanna get in on this?

30:37.305 --> 30:39.841
Some Dawson? Wanna get
some Dawson on you?

30:39.874 --> 30:41.609
No, I'm good. It's...

30:42.343 --> 30:43.578
Baby, it's 2:00 a.m.

30:44.012 --> 30:45.279
Okay.

30:45.780 --> 30:47.248
I'mma go to bed. <i>(SIGHS)</i>

30:47.281 --> 30:48.816
Let me know how it ends.

30:50.651 --> 30:51.719
All right.

30:54.089 --> 30:55.323
Goodnight.

30:56.058 --> 30:57.892
- I'll be right up.
- Okay.

30:59.061 --> 31:01.395
<i>Uh, cartoon bird, little Katie.</i>

31:01.429 --> 31:02.497
<i>Three answers remaining.</i>

31:02.530 --> 31:04.133
- KATIE: <i>Daffy Duck.</i>
- Um.

31:04.166 --> 31:05.399
RICHARD: <i>Let's see</i>
<i>if you made it.</i>

31:05.433 --> 31:08.770
It's late. I should
probably get some sleep.

31:08.803 --> 31:10.005
<i>(PEOPLE CHEERING ON TV)</i>

31:10.038 --> 31:11.073
<i>(REMOTE CLICKING)</i>

31:11.106 --> 31:12.507
This isn't working.

31:13.242 --> 31:15.576
- What?
- This isn't working.

31:16.611 --> 31:19.214
So I'm gonna need you
to pack your stuff

31:19.248 --> 31:20.481
and leave first thing in the morning

31:20.515 --> 31:22.017
before Cece wakes up.

31:22.850 --> 31:23.885
So she doesn't get upset.

31:23.919 --> 31:25.720
No, Nina.

31:26.922 --> 31:28.023
I... I...

31:28.056 --> 31:29.757
I didn't think anyone was
gonna be down here.

31:29.791 --> 31:31.425
You told me I could use
the screening room.

31:31.459 --> 31:33.195
I'm gonna need
the phone back as well.

31:33.228 --> 31:35.030
Please, Nina.

31:35.063 --> 31:37.032
- <i>(SCOFFING)</i>
- I will do anything

31:37.065 --> 31:38.766
to make it up to you.
I promise.

31:38.800 --> 31:39.867
Can you just give me...

31:40.735 --> 31:41.769
one more chance?

31:43.704 --> 31:44.772
<i>(NINA SIGHS)</i>

31:45.274 --> 31:46.507
Um...

31:47.009 --> 31:48.076
Fine.

31:49.644 --> 31:50.678
One week.

31:51.146 --> 31:52.547
Okay?

31:52.580 --> 31:55.349
But you're gonna
have to dress appropriately

31:55.383 --> 31:56.884
around the house from now on.

31:57.986 --> 31:59.520
Yeah, of course. Sorry.

32:05.359 --> 32:06.929
Oh, Millie.

32:09.430 --> 32:11.599
Stay the fuck away from my husband.

32:26.814 --> 32:28.549
<i>(OVEN DINGS)</i>

32:28.583 --> 32:30.418
- JILIANNE: Mmm.
- And so my nanny's going on

32:30.451 --> 32:32.620
and on about her dead dog,

32:32.653 --> 32:35.523
and I don't mean to be a B-I-T-C-H,

32:35.556 --> 32:38.359
but since when did I become
a canine grief counselor?

32:38.392 --> 32:40.728
Meanwhile, Emma is late for school.

32:40.761 --> 32:43.198
- WOMEN: Mmm.
- I'm missing yoga.

32:43.232 --> 32:44.498
You know what yoga means
to me.

32:44.532 --> 32:46.767
- It's everything.
- That's so unfortunate.

32:46.801 --> 32:47.903
Thank you.

32:47.936 --> 32:49.037
<i>(INHALES)</i>

32:49.071 --> 32:52.406
Well, we are going to be
looking for a nanny soon.

32:52.440 --> 32:54.475
<i>(GASPS)</i> Oh, my God, Nina!
You're pregnant.

32:54.508 --> 32:56.844
- Nina. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>
- I knew it.

32:56.878 --> 32:58.947
No. Not... Not yet.

32:58.981 --> 33:00.781
We are making a plan.

33:00.815 --> 33:02.483
We've been going to see
this incredible

33:02.516 --> 33:04.119
fertility specialist in the city.

33:04.152 --> 33:05.486
- Cool.
- Andrew insists

33:05.519 --> 33:07.089
on sparing no expense,

33:07.122 --> 33:08.689
of course. So, yeah.

33:08.723 --> 33:11.026
- That's wonderful.
- JILIANNE: Ooh, yeah.

33:11.059 --> 33:14.196
We will find you the most
fantastic nanny, I promise.

33:14.229 --> 33:15.563
- Absolutely.
- Thanks.

33:15.596 --> 33:17.865
Oh, this is Cece's pediatrician.

33:17.899 --> 33:20.068
- I will be right back.
- SUZANNE: Oh.

33:21.069 --> 33:22.403
Fill our tea.

33:25.640 --> 33:26.741
JILIANNE: Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.

33:26.774 --> 33:28.343
I really thought she was pregnant.

33:28.377 --> 33:29.443
I know, we were all thinking it.

33:29.477 --> 33:30.611
I mean, have you seen her skin?

33:30.645 --> 33:32.180
God, and how about those roots?

33:32.214 --> 33:33.348
My God. You'd think she would take

33:33.382 --> 33:35.150
better care of herself for Andrew.

33:35.183 --> 33:36.751
- He's so fucking hot.
- He is.

33:36.784 --> 33:39.354
And especially because
they have an airtight prenup.

33:39.388 --> 33:40.888
- JILIANNE: Mmm.
- Okay. You know,

33:40.923 --> 33:43.325
she did not have a dime
when they got married.

33:43.358 --> 33:44.659
She'll be sleeping on the street

33:44.692 --> 33:46.028
if she doesn't get her shit together.

33:46.061 --> 33:48.829
Cece? Would he get custody, considering...

33:48.863 --> 33:51.934
PATRICE: Of course.
After what she did.

33:51.967 --> 33:54.236
How many months she spent
in that awful psych ward?

33:54.269 --> 33:56.271
- JILIANNE AND SUZANNE: Nine.
- <i>(PATRICE CHUCKLING)</i> Nine.

33:56.305 --> 33:57.505
Nine months. <i>(SCOFFS)</i>

33:57.538 --> 33:58.839
I mean, good Lord,

33:58.873 --> 34:00.275
I do not know
how he puts up with her.

34:00.309 --> 34:02.476
PATRICE: Because he is a saint.

34:02.510 --> 34:03.912
- He's a hot saint.
- <i>(PATRICE EXCLAIMS)</i>

34:03.946 --> 34:07.448
- Hot Saint Andrew. Oh, my God.
- <i>(ALL CHUCKLING)</i>

34:07.481 --> 34:09.051
- SUZANNE: Ooh.
- What did I miss?

34:09.084 --> 34:12.120
Oh, we're just talking
spring fundraiser.

34:12.154 --> 34:13.188
- PATRICE: Ooh.
- Please,

34:13.221 --> 34:14.855
save us with a theme idea.

34:16.925 --> 34:18.961
Stop lurking.

34:18.994 --> 34:21.063
MILLIE: <i>Those women were right</i>
<i>about one thing.</i>

34:21.096 --> 34:23.932
<i>Andrew is definitely a saint</i>
<i>for standing by Nina.</i>

34:23.966 --> 34:26.368
<i>I can't believe she lied</i>
<i>about being pregnant.</i>

34:26.401 --> 34:28.569
<i>Everything she's told me</i>
<i>is a lie.</i>

34:28.602 --> 34:30.272
<i>It wasn't the hormones</i>
<i>making her crazy.</i>

34:30.305 --> 34:32.407
<i>She actually is crazy.</i>

34:32.441 --> 34:33.641
<i>Poor Andrew.</i>

34:33.674 --> 34:35.043
<i>As soon as I save up</i>
<i>enough money,</i>

34:35.077 --> 34:36.744
<i>I am out of here.</i>

34:39.314 --> 34:41.482
Today wasn't a total disaster.

34:42.217 --> 34:43.986
Uh, thank you.

34:44.019 --> 34:46.021
I'm gonna need you
to watch Cece next Saturday.

34:46.054 --> 34:48.589
Andrew and I have
an appointment in the city,

34:48.622 --> 34:49.992
and I know it's your day off,

34:50.025 --> 34:52.693
but I trust
that it won't be a problem.

34:52.727 --> 34:53.794
Uh...

34:54.729 --> 34:56.932
- We'll have fun.
- Good.

35:25.327 --> 35:26.995
Haloperidol.

35:32.134 --> 35:34.236
Acute fucking psychosis?

35:37.805 --> 35:39.874
<i>Hey, Lexi, it's Millie. Listen.</i>

35:39.908 --> 35:41.276
<i>I really need to make</i>
<i>some extra money</i>

35:41.309 --> 35:42.543
<i>so I can quit this job.</i>

35:42.576 --> 35:44.779
Do you think you could, um,
ask your cousin

35:44.812 --> 35:47.382
if I could get a job
at the warehouse?

35:47.416 --> 35:48.549
I'll do anything. I'll clean,

35:48.582 --> 35:50.052
I'll set boxes,
I'll scrub toilets.

35:50.085 --> 35:52.354
I just really need
to get out of here.

35:52.387 --> 35:54.189
You're leaving?

35:54.222 --> 35:55.257
What?

35:55.656 --> 35:57.325
No, no, no.

35:57.359 --> 35:58.927
I'm gonna...

35:58.960 --> 36:00.128
make you lunch.

36:01.329 --> 36:02.596
What are you in the mood for?

36:02.630 --> 36:04.166
A bologna sandwich?

36:04.832 --> 36:05.900
Okay.

36:05.934 --> 36:08.403
But you said you needed
to get out of this place

36:08.437 --> 36:09.504
on the phone just now.

36:09.538 --> 36:11.006
No.

36:11.039 --> 36:12.240
You misheard me.

36:14.575 --> 36:16.811
One bologna sandwich
coming right up.

36:19.448 --> 36:21.516
So how was, uh...

36:21.550 --> 36:22.984
how was school this week?

36:23.018 --> 36:26.555
Learn anything fun or interesting?

36:26.587 --> 36:29.690
It's school.
It's not fun or interesting.

36:30.392 --> 36:32.461
What about boys?

36:32.494 --> 36:34.129
- <i>(EXCLAIMS)</i>
- Got any crushes?

36:34.162 --> 36:36.498
Ew, no. Why would you even
ask me that?

36:36.531 --> 36:38.300
I am just...

36:38.333 --> 36:39.900
trying to make some small talk.

36:40.936 --> 36:42.370
Forget it.

36:42.404 --> 36:43.704
I'm not hungry anyway.

36:46.441 --> 36:47.909
Okay.

36:51.879 --> 36:53.781
You don't have to be
my friend, you know.

36:53.814 --> 36:55.517
It's not part of your job.

36:55.550 --> 36:57.385
Well, I'd like to be.

36:57.419 --> 36:58.786
Why?

36:58.819 --> 37:00.555
'Cause I like you.

37:00.589 --> 37:01.923
No, you don't.

37:05.560 --> 37:06.995
CECE: <i>"Do you want juice or water?"</i>

37:07.028 --> 37:08.363
"Juice, please."

37:08.396 --> 37:09.598
"Don't spill.

37:09.630 --> 37:11.066
"Juice is a privilege."

37:11.099 --> 37:13.401
"I won't."
"Did you go to the salon today?"

37:13.435 --> 37:14.735
"Yes."

37:14.768 --> 37:15.937
"You look very nice."

37:15.971 --> 37:18.540
- "Thank you."
- Cece, would you like some

37:18.573 --> 37:20.175
dinosaur chicken nuggets
and ketchup?

37:20.808 --> 37:22.277
Ketchup makes a mess.

37:22.310 --> 37:23.677
Yes, it does.

37:23.711 --> 37:24.946
<i>(CECE SIGHS)</i>

37:25.413 --> 37:26.814
<i>(MILLIE SIGHS)</i>

37:30.651 --> 37:32.686
Cece, where did you find
this troll?

37:34.356 --> 37:36.091
Were you in my room?

37:36.124 --> 37:38.493
Cece, this troll is
very special to me.

37:38.527 --> 37:40.761
I don't want you going into
my room, do you understand?

37:40.794 --> 37:42.631
You need to stay
out of the attic.

37:42.663 --> 37:44.765
- So do you.
- <i>(DOOR BANGING)</i>

37:44.798 --> 37:46.800
- ANDREW: Hey.
- <i>(NINA EXCLAIMING)</i>

37:47.768 --> 37:49.905
<i>(BREATH TREMBLING)</i>

37:49.938 --> 37:50.972
<i>(CRYING)</i>

37:52.240 --> 37:54.742
<i>(SIGHS)</i> Hey, Cece,

37:54.775 --> 37:55.809
can you go play
in your bedroom

37:55.843 --> 37:57.112
for a little bit, please?

38:00.448 --> 38:02.417
<i>(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)</i>

38:02.450 --> 38:03.652
- What happened?
- <i>(TEAPOT WHISTLING)</i>

38:03.684 --> 38:05.453
ANDREW: Premature ovarian insufficiency.

38:05.487 --> 38:06.820
We've been trying for years.

38:07.322 --> 38:08.957
At least now we know.

38:08.990 --> 38:10.791
- I'm sorry.
- I've just... <i>(SIGHS)</i>

38:10.824 --> 38:13.595
Man, I've just always wanted
a lot of kids.

38:13.628 --> 38:16.131
Like a... like a whole
soccer team full.

38:17.332 --> 38:19.467
<i>(CLEARS THROAT)</i> Nina and I
were only children like you.

38:19.501 --> 38:20.635
<i>(CABINET KNOB CLICKS)</i>

38:20.669 --> 38:21.903
Well, at least you have Cece.

38:21.937 --> 38:23.371
Of course, of course.

38:26.707 --> 38:28.310
I know it sounds selfish.

38:29.743 --> 38:31.413
I love Cece.

38:31.446 --> 38:33.814
I've always wanted a child
of my own with Nina.

38:33.847 --> 38:35.250
I didn't realize...

38:35.283 --> 38:39.387
Oh, Cece is...
she's absolutely my daughter.

38:40.222 --> 38:42.723
She's just not
my biological daughter.

38:42.756 --> 38:44.492
You're an amazing dad.

38:44.526 --> 38:47.295
Look, I just really don't know
how she's gonna take this.

38:47.329 --> 38:49.531
<i>(BREATHES DEEPLY)</i>

38:49.564 --> 38:51.132
She's been so fragile lately.

38:53.235 --> 38:57.172
I really don't think that she
can handle the disappointment.

38:57.205 --> 38:58.039
She has you.

38:58.073 --> 39:00.442
I don't think that I am enough.

39:04.613 --> 39:05.879
<i>(OBJECTS CLATTERING)</i>

39:14.623 --> 39:15.889
- <i>(NINA SCREAMING)</i>
- <i>(CLANKS)</i>

39:15.924 --> 39:18.927
NINA: It's not fair!
I did everything I could!

39:18.960 --> 39:20.662
ANDREW: Nina, it's not your fault.

39:20.695 --> 39:22.796
- <i>(SHATTERING)</i>
- NINA: You wish I was gone.

39:22.830 --> 39:24.065
ANDREW: God! Wait! Nina, no!

39:24.099 --> 39:25.233
- Hello?
- ANDREW: No, no, no!

39:25.267 --> 39:27.068
Andrew, are you...
are you okay?

39:28.570 --> 39:30.071
What?

39:32.873 --> 39:34.042
Oh, my God.

39:34.075 --> 39:37.212
- Andrew, are you okay?
- <i>(CHUCKLING)</i>

39:37.245 --> 39:39.948
What? You overheard
those PTA cunts

39:39.981 --> 39:41.549
saying that I'm crazy?

39:41.583 --> 39:43.851
That I don't deserve
my husband?

39:43.884 --> 39:46.154
That I belong in a nuthouse?

39:46.588 --> 39:47.956
Andrew!

39:53.827 --> 39:55.430
Let go of this.

39:57.232 --> 39:59.701
- Wrap this around your hand.
- Thank you.

39:59.734 --> 40:01.102
Alive and well.

40:13.548 --> 40:14.848
<i>(SPRAYING)</i>

40:18.253 --> 40:19.354
<i>(SPRAYING)</i>

40:26.928 --> 40:28.163
<i>(NINA SIGHS)</i>

40:29.130 --> 40:31.832
I cleaned up
the mess from last night.

40:33.702 --> 40:36.171
Sorry I wasn't honest
about the baby.

40:37.806 --> 40:39.441
I guess I was...

40:39.474 --> 40:41.142
trying to manifest.

40:42.410 --> 40:43.578
Or something.

40:46.047 --> 40:47.749
It's okay, I get it. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

40:47.782 --> 40:51.619
I don't know... <i>(CHUCKLING)</i>
...how I'm gonna face Andrew's mother.

40:55.856 --> 40:57.125
Anyway,

40:58.059 --> 41:00.395
I realized I need to stop
holding onto things

41:00.428 --> 41:02.263
and just start fresh.

41:02.297 --> 41:04.833
So these are
practically brand-new,

41:04.865 --> 41:06.968
and I want you to have them.

41:08.370 --> 41:09.404
I...

41:09.838 --> 41:11.339
I... I can't.

41:11.373 --> 41:12.474
No, seriously,

41:12.507 --> 41:14.809
these are gonna be thrown
in the bin at Goodwill.

41:14.843 --> 41:16.877
This would look amazing on you.

41:17.479 --> 41:19.147
Millie, take it.

41:19.880 --> 41:21.082
Thanks.

41:21.116 --> 41:23.284
Well, Andrew took Cece
to pancakes,

41:23.318 --> 41:26.554
so you don't really have to
worry about breakfast this morning.

41:26.588 --> 41:28.690
But I do need a favor.

41:28.723 --> 41:32.093
I need you to look into tickets
for a musical called <i>Showdown.</i>

41:32.893 --> 41:35.563
Andrew's been dying to see it,

41:35.597 --> 41:37.898
and I want to do something to

41:37.932 --> 41:39.900
make it up to him.

41:40.568 --> 41:41.803
Sure. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

41:41.836 --> 41:43.204
This Saturday,

41:43.738 --> 41:45.407
if you can manage,

41:45.440 --> 41:48.676
and an overnight at a high-end hotel.

41:48.710 --> 41:49.811
Splurge on a suite.

41:49.844 --> 41:52.013
Something romantic.

41:52.046 --> 41:54.783
And Cece will be
at a friend's house.

41:54.816 --> 41:56.418
I'll arrange for her to...

41:57.719 --> 41:58.953
uh, be out of the house

41:58.987 --> 42:01.689
and you can just have
the weekend to yourself.

42:02.424 --> 42:04.426
That sounds great.

42:04.459 --> 42:06.227
I'll see what I can do.

42:06.261 --> 42:08.263
You're a lifesaver, Millie.

42:10.031 --> 42:12.233
I don't know what I'd do without you.

42:12.634 --> 42:13.935
<i>(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)</i>

42:13.968 --> 42:17.972
<i>(PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)</i>

42:18.940 --> 42:20.308
<i>(EXHALES)</i>

42:23.945 --> 42:26.281
You're with
the Winchesters, right?

42:26.314 --> 42:28.983
- Yeah.
- I'm with the Leightons.

42:30.218 --> 42:31.386
Suzanne?

42:31.419 --> 42:32.487
Right.

42:33.688 --> 42:36.424
Cece's not that good, is she?

42:37.459 --> 42:38.993
<i>(LAUGHS)</i>

42:39.027 --> 42:41.563
Don't worry.
No one gives her any shit.

42:41.596 --> 42:43.731
Not after everything
she's been through.

42:45.133 --> 42:46.568
What do you mean?

42:46.936 --> 42:48.002
Seriously?

42:48.036 --> 42:50.138
All the psycho mom shit?

42:50.171 --> 42:52.707
I know she spent some time
in a psych ward, but...

42:55.477 --> 42:56.511
Um...

42:59.180 --> 43:03.384
Nina Winchester tried
to drown her kid in a bathtub.

43:04.118 --> 43:05.320
- What?
- Yeah.

43:05.353 --> 43:07.856
It's like all the PTA bitches
talk about.

43:07.889 --> 43:09.959
When Cece was a baby,

43:09.991 --> 43:12.928
Nina threw her
in a tub of running water,

43:12.962 --> 43:14.229
then tried to off herself

43:14.262 --> 43:16.498
by swallowing
a shit ton of pills.

43:16.531 --> 43:18.833
Luckily, her husband got freaked out

43:18.867 --> 43:20.368
when he couldn't get
ahold of her,

43:20.401 --> 43:23.338
then called the police
for a wellness check.

43:23.371 --> 43:27.242
It's, like, fucked up, right?

43:27.275 --> 43:30.178
INSTRUCTOR: Great job,
dancers. Thank you.

43:30.211 --> 43:32.647
- Let's get our belongings.
- GIRL: All right.

43:36.986 --> 43:38.553
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

43:44.225 --> 43:46.761
- Your car smells like feet.
- Thank you.

43:51.566 --> 43:52.600
Hey.

43:54.402 --> 43:56.638
What do you know about this family?

43:56.671 --> 43:57.805
Sorry, no English.

43:57.839 --> 43:59.207
Oh, bullshit.

44:01.209 --> 44:02.777
I know you shouldn't be here.

44:02.810 --> 44:05.446
- <i>(DOOR OPENS)</i>
- Why?

44:06.648 --> 44:07.749
NINA: Leave him alone.

44:07.782 --> 44:08.816
<i>(DOOR CLOSES)</i>

44:10.920 --> 44:13.221
You've no business
talking to Enzo.

44:13.989 --> 44:16.591
<i>(SCOFFS)</i> What is this?

44:16.624 --> 44:19.594
They're the Broadway tickets
and the hotel reservation.

44:19.627 --> 44:21.396
- For Saturday?
- Yeah.

44:21.429 --> 44:24.599
But why would I have you
book tickets...

44:24.632 --> 44:27.468
for the day that I'm driving
Cece to arts camp in D.C.?

44:27.502 --> 44:30.039
- Why would I do that?
- I don't know, but you did.

44:30.071 --> 44:31.873
No, I didn't.

44:31.907 --> 44:35.543
And I assume that these are
non-refundable now, at this point?

44:35.577 --> 44:37.779
Nina, I did what you asked me to do.

44:37.812 --> 44:39.781
Fine. They're gonna
come out of your paycheck.

44:39.814 --> 44:41.951
And I'm so sorry about that,
but it was your mistake,

44:41.984 --> 44:43.885
and you're gonna
have to cover the fee.

44:43.919 --> 44:45.553
Nina, I can't afford that.

44:45.587 --> 44:46.588
I don't care!

44:46.621 --> 44:48.189
It was your mistake.
You're gonna cover it.

44:48.222 --> 44:50.258
Nina, that's more than I have saved.

44:50.291 --> 44:51.927
Hey.

44:51.961 --> 44:53.394
- Hello.
- NINA: Hi.

44:56.932 --> 44:58.333
Just about cleaned out the florist,

44:58.366 --> 45:01.102
so otherwise I would have...
I would have got you more.

45:01.769 --> 45:03.104
What's wrong?

45:03.805 --> 45:05.139
Millie booked tickets

45:05.173 --> 45:07.308
for a non-refundable weekend for us

45:07.342 --> 45:10.144
that we can't even use.

45:10.178 --> 45:12.347
And she's gonna have
to pay for it. Sorry.

45:12.380 --> 45:13.881
No, she doesn't. That's okay.

45:13.916 --> 45:15.817
We'll just call the credit card
company and have it reversed.

45:15.850 --> 45:17.086
I don't think that's a thing.

45:17.118 --> 45:19.320
ANDREW: That is a thing.
That's a thing.

45:19.354 --> 45:21.522
You don't have to pay for anything.

45:21.889 --> 45:23.157
Thank you.

45:23.691 --> 45:25.193
I'm sorry.

45:29.564 --> 45:30.665
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

45:33.735 --> 45:34.869
Sweetheart?

45:42.744 --> 45:44.412
<i>(SOFT THUDS)</i>

45:44.445 --> 45:45.880
ANDREW: All this stuff
for a week?

45:45.914 --> 45:48.282
I don't want her to get homesick.

45:51.219 --> 45:52.720
<i>(ENGINE STARTS)</i>

45:55.223 --> 45:58.459
<i>(WATER RUNNING)</i>

46:15.110 --> 46:17.578
Okay. Sorry. Shit. Okay.

46:17.946 --> 46:19.213
Sorry.

46:26.721 --> 46:29.891
I am so sorry. I usually get
dressed before I come out.

46:29.925 --> 46:32.694
No, it's really my fault.
I was actually just...

46:32.727 --> 46:35.329
I was coming to confess
something to you.

46:37.032 --> 46:40.635
I wanted to let you know that
I couldn't get the tickets refunded.

46:41.369 --> 46:43.271
- Shit.
- Yeah.

46:46.340 --> 46:49.011
So I think you should take them

46:49.044 --> 46:50.778
and go to the show with a friend

46:50.812 --> 46:53.214
and stay in the room,
charge whatever you want.

46:53.247 --> 46:55.850
Room service.
I want you to enjoy yourself.

46:56.751 --> 46:58.286
That is...

46:58.319 --> 47:01.190
really nice of you, but...

47:01.222 --> 47:03.725
I can't. I don't have anyone
I can bring.

47:03.758 --> 47:05.660
You gotta have somebody.

47:07.528 --> 47:09.430
I wish I did, but I don't.

47:10.598 --> 47:11.934
<i>(ANDREW SIGHS)</i>

47:15.436 --> 47:18.506
Okay, well, just, um...
how about you and I go?

47:19.574 --> 47:22.343
We can come back tonight.
I can...

47:23.277 --> 47:24.579
I can sweeten the deal a little bit,

47:24.612 --> 47:27.648
throw in a slice of pizza,
maybe a hot apple cider?

47:28.316 --> 47:30.485
I'll just tell Nina that I...

47:30.518 --> 47:32.854
exchanged the tickets
and I can take her next week.

47:32.887 --> 47:34.822
No, I can't have you do that.

47:34.856 --> 47:37.092
Oh, come on, we could both
use a night out.

47:37.126 --> 47:39.761
I know we could. Why not?

47:39.794 --> 47:42.330
I mean, it's supposed to be
a great show.

47:43.966 --> 47:45.033
Okay.

47:46.267 --> 47:48.469
Great. We're going.

47:51.073 --> 47:53.374
<i>("CINNAMON GIRL"
BY LANA DEL REY PLAYING)</i>

47:53.407 --> 47:54.977
<i>♪ Cinnamon ♪</i>

47:57.179 --> 47:59.347
<i>♪ In my teeth ♪</i>

48:00.548 --> 48:02.884
<i>♪ From your kiss ♪</i>

48:03.952 --> 48:06.754
<i>♪ You're touching me ♪</i>

48:06.788 --> 48:08.056
Great dress.

48:08.090 --> 48:10.291
<i>♪ All the pills ♪</i>

48:11.059 --> 48:13.494
<i>♪ That you take ♪</i>

48:13.528 --> 48:17.032
<i>♪ Violet, blue, green</i>
<i>red to keep me ♪</i>

48:17.065 --> 48:20.535
<i>♪ At arm's length don't work ♪</i>

48:20.568 --> 48:23.105
<i>♪ You try to push me out ♪</i>

48:23.138 --> 48:24.940
<i>♪ But I just find my... ♪</i>

48:24.973 --> 48:27.242
Thanks for coming.

48:27.276 --> 48:32.580
<i>♪ Violet, blue, green, red</i>
<i>to keep me out, I win ♪</i>

48:32.613 --> 48:36.118
<i>♪ There's things</i>
<i>I wanna say to you ♪</i>

48:36.151 --> 48:38.954
<i>♪ But I'll just let you live ♪</i>

48:38.987 --> 48:42.723
<i>♪ Like if you hold me</i>
<i>without hurting me ♪</i>

48:42.757 --> 48:46.261
<i>♪ You'll be the first</i>
<i>who ever did ♪</i>

48:46.295 --> 48:49.764
<i>♪ There's things</i>
<i>I wanna talk about ♪</i>

48:49.797 --> 48:52.935
<i>♪ But better not to give ♪</i>

48:52.968 --> 48:56.838
<i>♪ But if you hold me</i>
<i>without hurting me ♪</i>

48:56.871 --> 49:00.741
<i>♪ You'll be the first</i>
<i>who ever did ♪</i>

49:07.882 --> 49:10.818
<i>♪ Be the first who ever did ♪</i>

49:12.154 --> 49:13.554
- I'm hungry.
- Yeah, I'm hungry.

49:13.588 --> 49:15.823
- I could eat. Yeah.
- Yeah? <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

49:15.857 --> 49:17.491
Wasn't pizza
a part of this deal?

49:17.525 --> 49:19.061
- Yeah, it was.
- Yeah?

49:19.094 --> 49:22.597
Yeah. You know what?
I think I got a better idea.

49:22.630 --> 49:24.233
MILLIE: Holy shit,
that was amazing.

49:24.266 --> 49:25.399
<i>(ANDREW SIGHS)</i>

49:25.433 --> 49:26.901
- It was, wasn't it?
- Yeah.

49:26.935 --> 49:28.003
ANDREW: Yeah.

49:29.271 --> 49:31.505
MILLIE: This place is really fancy.

49:31.539 --> 49:33.242
Well, it's charming,

49:33.275 --> 49:34.910
in an old New York kind of way.

49:34.943 --> 49:36.311
Yeah.

49:36.345 --> 49:37.712
I... I don't...

49:37.745 --> 49:39.413
<i>(CHUCKLING)</i> I don't really
know what I should order.

49:39.447 --> 49:41.316
Well, how about we just get
one of everything?

49:41.350 --> 49:42.583
- Everything?
- Everything.

49:42.617 --> 49:45.486
- <i>(CHUCKLING)</i> We can't do that.
- Yeah, we can.

49:48.456 --> 49:49.824
You like martinis?

49:50.391 --> 49:51.559
I guess. I don't know.

49:51.592 --> 49:53.461
- Well, I guess we'll find out.
- Yeah.

49:53.494 --> 49:54.862
To new adventures.

49:54.896 --> 49:55.998
Cheers.

50:00.902 --> 50:02.237
ANDREW: I mean,
you're funny, you're...

50:02.271 --> 50:03.738
you're caring,
you're great with kids.

50:03.771 --> 50:05.806
I just don't understand why
you're cleaning people's houses.

50:05.840 --> 50:08.377
You should be out there
living your best life.

50:08.409 --> 50:09.978
And have you ever thought
about what

50:10.012 --> 50:13.015
you want to do with your time
on this Earth?

50:13.881 --> 50:17.152
- I don't know. No, not really.
- Why not?

50:17.986 --> 50:19.321
<i>(MILLIE INHALES)</i>

50:19.354 --> 50:20.454
What about you?

50:20.488 --> 50:21.789
Are you...

50:21.822 --> 50:24.558
living your best life doing...

50:24.592 --> 50:26.460
I don't even know what you do.

50:26.494 --> 50:28.163
I run a data processing company

50:28.196 --> 50:30.232
that my father left me.

50:30.265 --> 50:32.267
Basically, I get paid
a lot of money

50:32.301 --> 50:34.669
to do really boring shit.

50:34.702 --> 50:37.438
- Gotcha.
- I mean, all I've ever really wanted to do

50:37.471 --> 50:40.075
was to be a husband
and a father, honestly.

50:40.608 --> 50:42.411
That's really sweet.

50:42.443 --> 50:44.745
What about you? Do you want kids?

50:45.813 --> 50:46.881
Yeah.

50:47.382 --> 50:48.616
Someday.

50:49.617 --> 50:51.552
With the right person, of course.

50:52.087 --> 50:53.322
I mean, I... I...

50:53.355 --> 50:55.589
feel like I won the lottery
with Nina, and I should feel

50:55.623 --> 50:58.093
- like I'm living my best life.
- But you're not?

50:58.126 --> 50:59.794
I love my wife.

50:59.827 --> 51:01.529
I really do.

51:01.562 --> 51:03.597
I just feel like
she's angry all the time,

51:03.631 --> 51:05.067
and I don't know why.

51:05.100 --> 51:07.902
I feel like every conversation
we have ends in a tirade.

51:08.904 --> 51:11.772
If it makes you feel
any better, same. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

51:11.806 --> 51:15.010
I mean, she used to be
so different. She was, uh...

51:15.043 --> 51:16.811
She was... loving,

51:16.844 --> 51:19.114
and she was kind,
and she was generous.

51:19.714 --> 51:21.450
She was affectionate.

51:21.482 --> 51:24.152
I mean, all I want to do is
make her happy

51:24.186 --> 51:26.088
and I genuinely don't know how.

51:26.121 --> 51:27.788
Andrew, it's not you.

51:28.991 --> 51:30.926
I should not have said that.
I'm sorry.

51:30.959 --> 51:32.560
No, it's okay. I mean, I see
the way that she treats you,

51:32.593 --> 51:34.262
and I hate it.

51:36.164 --> 51:37.232
I hate it.

51:38.833 --> 51:41.103
I feel like I'm letting you down.

51:41.836 --> 51:42.870
You're not.

51:48.443 --> 51:50.678
Pretty sure there's
a dance floor in there.

51:53.115 --> 51:54.116
<i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

51:54.149 --> 51:56.485
- You want to go dancing?
- Should we hit it?

51:56.517 --> 51:58.086
<i>(CHUCKLING)</i>

51:58.120 --> 51:59.187
Yeah.

52:00.489 --> 52:01.722
Let's dance.

52:01.756 --> 52:06.727
<i>♪ Will your eyes</i>
<i>return to mine? ♪</i>

52:08.529 --> 52:12.566
<i>♪ Will our day start to shine? ♪</i>

52:13.235 --> 52:15.070
<i>♪ It was winter ♪</i>

52:15.103 --> 52:22.144
<i>♪ Now let's move</i>
<i>right into spring ♪</i>

52:22.177 --> 52:25.780
<i>♪ Let the birds sing ♪</i>

52:29.017 --> 52:30.952
<i>(FAINT CLAPPING)</i>

52:30.986 --> 52:32.553
<i>(ANDREW CHUCKLES)</i>

52:33.922 --> 52:37.259
I don't suppose you feel sober
enough to drive us home?

52:38.360 --> 52:39.860
Not really, no.

52:40.861 --> 52:42.297
I think we got a problem.

52:46.001 --> 52:49.770
RECEPTIONIST: And you're all set.

52:49.804 --> 52:51.739
They're not adjoining,
but they're on the same floor.

52:51.772 --> 52:54.142
- Thanks.
- ANDREW: Mm.

52:54.176 --> 52:55.277
Shit, my phone's dead.

52:55.310 --> 52:56.610
Oh.

52:57.578 --> 52:58.879
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

52:58.914 --> 53:01.615
- Of course. Have a great stay.
- Thank you.

53:01.649 --> 53:03.717
<i>(THUNDER RUMBLING)</i>

53:06.188 --> 53:07.755
<i>(ELEVATOR DINGS)</i>

53:29.511 --> 53:31.179
I'll see you in the morning.

53:33.248 --> 53:34.648
Good night.

53:51.066 --> 53:52.167
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

53:52.934 --> 53:53.969
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

53:58.273 --> 53:59.307
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

54:01.076 --> 54:02.643
<i>(WATER RUNNING)</i>

54:08.517 --> 54:11.019
Do not blow up your life.

54:11.052 --> 54:13.455
- <i>(THUNDER RUMBLING)</i>
- <i>(SIGHS)</i>

54:13.488 --> 54:15.257
<i>(PHONE VIBRATING)</i>

54:22.230 --> 54:23.431
Oh, shit.

54:23.465 --> 54:25.699
<i>(THUNDERCLAP)</i>

54:26.468 --> 54:27.768
<i>(GASPS)</i>

54:28.203 --> 54:29.538
Oh, no.

54:29.571 --> 54:32.207
- <i>(KNOCKING AT DOOR)</i>
- Hey.

54:33.108 --> 54:34.342
What's wrong?

54:38.879 --> 54:40.748
She doesn't mean it.
I'll talk to her.

54:40.781 --> 54:43.051
- She does, Andrew. She does.
- Millie, come here.

54:43.084 --> 54:44.718
<i>(VOICE SHAKING)</i> She wants
to destroy my life,

54:44.752 --> 54:46.021
and I don't know why.

54:46.054 --> 54:48.756
No, she doesn't.
I will talk to her.

54:48.789 --> 54:51.226
Andrew, I know you think
that I can do better,

54:51.259 --> 54:53.028
but I need this job.

54:53.061 --> 54:55.863
I can't lose it. I... I...
I do not want to go back.

54:55.896 --> 54:59.668
- Go back where?
- <i>(THUNDER RUMBLING)</i>

54:59.700 --> 55:01.102
You're not going to lose your job.

55:01.136 --> 55:03.171
Everything is going to be okay.

55:04.039 --> 55:05.974
- I promise you.
- <i>(SNIFFLES)</i>

55:06.007 --> 55:07.209
Okay?

55:08.577 --> 55:11.146
Don't cry. It's okay.

55:11.179 --> 55:12.314
It's gonna be okay.

55:12.347 --> 55:13.747
<i>(MILLIE SIGHS)</i>

55:14.416 --> 55:15.816
<i>(THUNDER RUMBLING)</i>

55:15.849 --> 55:17.118
<i>("BAD AS THE REST"
BY JESSIE MURPH PLAYING)</i>

55:17.152 --> 55:19.654
<i>♪ Fool me once</i>
<i>and it's "So what?" ♪</i>

55:19.688 --> 55:22.123
<i>♪ Fool me twice</i>
<i>I'm a dumb fuck ♪</i>

55:22.157 --> 55:25.660
<i>♪ Three times, you like</i>
<i>every damn boy I ever loved ♪</i>

55:25.694 --> 55:27.028
<i>♪ Oh, no ♪</i>

55:27.062 --> 55:29.197
<i>(MILLIE MOANS)</i> Take off my dress.

55:29.231 --> 55:31.799
<i>♪ You're telling me</i>
<i>that you're the exception ♪</i>

55:31.832 --> 55:33.867
<i>♪ If you a good boy</i>
<i>with bad intentions ♪</i>

55:33.901 --> 55:35.203
<i>(ZIPPER UNZIPPING)</i>

55:35.237 --> 55:37.706
<i>♪ Tell me now ♪</i>

55:37.738 --> 55:39.908
<i>♪ 'Cause it's kinda late ♪</i>

55:39.941 --> 55:42.577
<i>♪ And I'm emotionally ♪</i>

55:42.611 --> 55:46.414
<i>♪ Kinda twisted right around ♪</i>

55:46.448 --> 55:48.882
<i>♪ And if I stay</i>
<i>another minute, babe ♪</i>

55:48.917 --> 55:51.453
<i>♪ I'll say a thing</i>
<i>I never say ♪</i>

55:51.486 --> 55:55.190
<i>♪ 'Cause something</i>
<i>'bout you breaks me down ♪</i>

55:55.223 --> 56:00.061
<i>♪ I do not love you yet ♪</i>

56:00.095 --> 56:04.966
<i>♪ But I'm 'bout</i>
<i>as close as I can get ♪</i>

56:05.000 --> 56:07.636
<i>♪ Keep one last percent ♪</i>

56:07.669 --> 56:09.971
<i>♪ Close to my chest ♪</i>

56:10.005 --> 56:15.043
<i>♪ Just in case</i>
<i>you turn out bad as the rest ♪</i>

56:15.076 --> 56:19.648
<i>♪ I will not be a fool ♪</i>

56:19.681 --> 56:24.885
<i>♪ But for you, I might do</i>
<i>what dumb bitches do ♪</i>

56:24.919 --> 56:27.322
<i>♪ Put on the dress say... ♪</i>

56:27.355 --> 56:29.157
<i>(MOANS SOFTLY)</i>

56:29.758 --> 56:31.293
<i>(THUNDERCLAP)</i>

56:31.326 --> 56:34.062
<i>♪ ...heart</i>
<i>from my place to your bed ♪</i>

56:34.095 --> 56:37.831
<i>♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪</i>

56:38.300 --> 56:40.201
<i>(THUNDERCLAP)</i>

56:44.506 --> 56:50.312
<i>♪ I'm as bad as the rest ♪</i>

56:58.486 --> 57:00.155
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

57:02.023 --> 57:03.558
Nina's coming home early.

57:04.926 --> 57:06.594
So we have to beat her home.

57:08.596 --> 57:09.931
We should get going.

57:10.498 --> 57:12.000
- Okay.
- Okay?

57:13.834 --> 57:15.437
This is gonna sound
really cheesy,

57:15.470 --> 57:19.140
but I didn't think anybody could
look so beautiful in the morning.

57:29.117 --> 57:30.884
Nina can't ever know.

57:32.053 --> 57:34.723
And this can't ever happen again.

57:34.756 --> 57:36.958
I really wish things were different.

57:38.193 --> 57:40.628
I wish I would have met you before.

57:42.097 --> 57:43.131
Me too.

57:43.665 --> 57:44.898
Are you okay?

57:45.367 --> 57:46.501
Yeah.

57:51.606 --> 57:53.041
<i>(SIGHS)</i>

58:15.764 --> 58:17.265
Nina?

58:22.470 --> 58:23.605
Nina!

58:25.473 --> 58:28.476
I'm gonna go get changed.

58:28.510 --> 58:31.479
I'll start making lunch
just in case she comes back.

58:49.330 --> 58:51.166
Ah, fuck it.

59:16.591 --> 59:17.625
Hello?

59:20.428 --> 59:21.496
Anybody home?

59:24.566 --> 59:25.700
<i>(OVEN DINGS)</i>

59:26.734 --> 59:28.102
Hi.

59:28.770 --> 59:30.805
Welcome home.

59:30.839 --> 59:33.641
- Thank you.
- Lunch is almost ready.

59:34.275 --> 59:36.144
Oh, boy.

59:36.678 --> 59:39.147
- Hi.
- Hey, sweetheart.

59:39.180 --> 59:42.183
- Hi. What are you doing?
- I was just fixing the drain

59:42.217 --> 59:44.786
in the upstairs guest bathroom.
It's a bit clogged.

59:44.819 --> 59:46.254
I knew you would try to do that.

59:46.287 --> 59:47.722
I said the plumber's coming
on Tuesday.

59:47.755 --> 59:49.657
No, I know. I was just
feeling extra manly today.

59:49.691 --> 59:51.793
- Okay.
- Yeah.

59:51.826 --> 59:53.428
How was the trip? How's Cece?

59:53.461 --> 59:55.063
She's good.

59:56.397 --> 59:58.099
Listen.

59:58.132 --> 01:00:00.034
I'm very sorry about last night.

01:00:01.035 --> 01:00:02.704
It was a very long drive.

01:00:02.737 --> 01:00:04.138
I was very tired. <i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

01:00:04.172 --> 01:00:06.407
I do not sleep well in hotels,

01:00:06.441 --> 01:00:07.475
turns out.

01:00:07.509 --> 01:00:10.111
And I should not be left alone
with my phone.

01:00:10.144 --> 01:00:13.715
So, lesson learned.
It's a new day.

01:00:13.748 --> 01:00:16.351
- Please accept my apologies.
- Yeah, it's okay.

01:00:16.384 --> 01:00:18.353
- I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.
- It's okay.

01:00:18.386 --> 01:00:20.522
- <i>(EXHALES)</i>
- Let's get some food in ya.

01:00:20.555 --> 01:00:21.456
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:00:21.489 --> 01:00:24.092
- NINA: Mm. Mm.
- NINA AND ANDREW: Hi.

01:00:24.893 --> 01:00:27.028
- This looks fantastic.
- Yes.

01:00:28.763 --> 01:00:30.832
<i>(BREATHES DEEPLY)</i>

01:00:30.865 --> 01:00:32.834
...you know? Hey, Millie.

01:00:32.867 --> 01:00:35.537
- MILLIE: Mm-hmm.
- How was your night off?

01:00:36.939 --> 01:00:39.407
Uh, my best friend Lexi took me

01:00:39.440 --> 01:00:41.809
- to Peter Luger.
- ANDREW: Hmm.

01:00:41.843 --> 01:00:44.013
Um, she had a gift certificate.
It was really nice.

01:00:44.045 --> 01:00:45.813
We had a lot of sides.

01:00:45.847 --> 01:00:47.048
<i>(CHUCKLES)</i>

01:00:47.081 --> 01:00:49.018
But I don't really eat meat.

01:00:49.050 --> 01:00:51.319
This looks incredible.
So, thank you.

01:00:51.352 --> 01:00:54.990
I don't know why
but my quiches never turn out.

01:00:55.024 --> 01:00:56.391
I've been meaning to ask you.

01:00:56.424 --> 01:00:58.693
Did you learn how to cook
while you were in prison?

01:01:01.563 --> 01:01:03.364
You know, she was in prison
for ten years

01:01:03.398 --> 01:01:05.400
before she came to work with us.

01:01:06.467 --> 01:01:07.735
Right?

01:01:08.803 --> 01:01:10.138
I think it's brave,

01:01:11.006 --> 01:01:14.509
making a new start in a new town.

